<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Destruction Warlock Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>DPS trinkets are very straightforward, as their performance is not affected by Warlock-specific buffs. As a result, direct-damage trinkets should generally be used on cooldown unless timed with specific boss mechanics that increase damage taken. Stat-increasing trinkets should similarly either be used on cooldown or aligned with burst phases (e.g., <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=113858/dark-soul-instability">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Soul: Instability</span></a>).<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>While the specific type of trinket (active vs. passive) isn't overly critical for Warlocks, passive trinkets are inherently easier to use and maintain uptime on, making them ideal for players who may forget to use actives or have inconsistent cooldown alignment.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96785/wushoolays-final-choice">
<img alt="Wushoolay's Final Choice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_chainlightning.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wushoolay's Final Choice</span></a> is our best-in-slot Phase 3 trinket. It offers a large amount of Hit rating and a powerful Intellect proc that stacks. Dropped by <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=69132/high-priestess-marli">
<span class="tinyicontxt">High Priestess Mar'li</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96827/breath-of-the-hydra">
<img alt="Breath of the Hydra" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_mindflay.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breath of the Hydra</span></a> is one of the strongest trinkets. It offers a large amount of Haste and a powerful Intellect proc. Dropped by <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=70212/flaming-head">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Flaming Head</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96930/unerring-vision-of-lei-shen">
<img alt="Unerring Vision of Lei Shen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_focusedaim.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unerring Vision of Lei Shen</span></a> is an excellent trinket option thanks to its powerful proc, granting 100% Critical Strike Chance for 4 seconds. It also provides a large amount of passive Intellect. Dropped by <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=68397/lei-shen">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96888/cha-yes-essence-of-brilliance">
<img alt="Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindsooth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cha-Ye's Essence of Brilliance</span></a> is one of the strongest pre-Siege trinkets available, providing Critical Strike as its passive and a powerful Intellect proc. With a proc rate scaling with your Critical Strike chance, it offers high uptime and excellent synergy for classes that naturally stack Crit. Dropped by <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=69427/dark-animus">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Animus</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
