<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gear_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Destruction Warlocks</span></h2>Professions in Mists of Pandaria offer a variety of bonuses, but their overall power is more balanced compared to previous expansions. Most profession bonuses amount to roughly +320 primary stat or a comparable bonus for secondary stats. You should avoid gathering professions (except Herbalism) when raiding, as they offer weaker or less consistent bonuses than crafting professions. Those looking to min-max will want to combine the short cooldown <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> from Engineering with the proc potential <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> of Tailoring. Below are the best options for Destruction Warlocks, focusing on Intellect, secondary stats, and sustained DPS.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Destruction Warlocks</h4>Engineering offers unique utility and burst potential through glove tinkers and movement tools. Deciding for yourself when the buff happens increases its utility, as it can be matched with other procs or cooldowns for more synergy.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126734/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_elementaloath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> provides +1920 Intellect for 10 seconds (60s cooldown), aligning perfectly with cooldowns like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=113858/dark-soul-instability">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Soul: Instability</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126389/goblin-glider">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_clothscrap_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Goblin Glider</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142568/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_burningspeed.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> can aid in movement-heavy fights.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Destruction Warlocks</h4>Tailoring remains a top choice for cloth casters due to its powerful cloak enchantment.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=142173/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> grants +2000 Intellect for 15 seconds with a 60s ICD, averaging ~320 Intellect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125496/masters-spellthread">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_astralrecalgroup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Master's Spellthread</span></a> is a cheaper alternative for <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82445/greater-cerulean-spellthread">
<img alt="Greater Cerulean Spellthread" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_42.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greater Cerulean Spellthread</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="herbalism">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_herbalism.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Herbalism for Destruction Warlocks</h4>Herbalism is the only gathering profession with a significant bonus. This is due to <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=121279/lifeblood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_wispsplodegreen.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifeblood</span></a>, an on-use Haste cooldown. Making it perfect for snapshotting with other strong procs. This mostly comes into play at higher item levels when plenty of base Intellect is already on gear.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=121279/lifeblood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_wispsplodegreen.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifeblood</span></a> now grants a Haste boost (2880 for 20s), helpful in snapshotting DoTs and burst damage.</div></li></ul>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c9" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_thread_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Destruction Warlocks</span></h3>Although not very powerful when compared to other options that are available in Phase 3, there are a few crafted items that can help you get started in your gearing journey:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94278/falling-blossom-cowl">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Cowl" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Cowl</span></a> is a strong crafted helm option for Warlocks, featuring valuable secondary stats with both Hit and Mastery. The high base Intellect and Stamina make it a durable and well-rounded choice before obtaining raid gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94277/falling-blossom-treads">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_cloth_raidmage_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Treads</span></a> is a solid crafted option for  Warlocks, offering a combination of Hit and Mastery. With two Red sockets and a Mastery socket bonus, they provide excellent gemming flexibility to boost key stats further.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82437/spelltwisters-grand-robe">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Grand Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Grand Robe</span></a> has good stats for Destruction Warlock, offering plenty of Haste and Mastery. Also, due to its higher item level, it helps you queue into Heroic and Celestial Dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82438/spelltwisters-gloves">
<img alt="Spelltwister's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_raidmage_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spelltwister's Gloves</span></a> has plenty of Hit. It is welcome since it allows you to reach the Hit Cap more easily. Same as with the same set chestpiece, it also increases your item level a fair bit early on, allowing you to queue into Heroic and Celestial Dungeons faster.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> from Engineering allows you to pick the secondary stats you want using Tinker's Gears, such as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77545/rigid-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Rigid Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Tinker's Gear</span></a>, alongside its equally high item level, considering the point in the game you can get it. This makes it a strong, early-crafted option.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79334/inscribed-jade-fan">
<img alt="Inscribed Jade Fan" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_1h_pandariatradeskill_c_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Jade Fan</span></a> originates from Inscription, but you can obtain it from other players or through the auction house. Not powerful on its own, but it enables stronger Main Hand + Off-Hand combos over staves.</div></li></ul>
